# AirPlay 1 audio receiver.
#
# Not started at boot: it holds a listening socket and advertises the box on
# the network, which should be something the user turns on. The controlling
# app sets persist.jetsontv.airplay.enabled and init does the rest, so nothing
# needs permission to exec a system binary.
#
# It runs as its own uid, system_ext_airplay (defined in device/nvidia/porg's
# config.fs), and specifically not as audioserver. libaudioclient decides by
# uid whether it is running *inside* audioserver: with that uid, AudioSystem
# skips the binder lookup for AudioFlinger and AudioPolicyService and waits
# INT32_MAX ms for an in-process service that never arrives, so the daemon hung
# in AAudioStreamBuilder_openStream on every stream -- no error, no denial, no
# sound. Not media either: audioserver trusts media to attribute tracks and
# recordings to other uids, which a daemon parsing network input should not be
# able to do.
#
# inet is the only group it needs, for its sockets. AAudio is a binder client,
# so neither audio nor media is required, and it opens no raw sockets.

# The metadata pipe lives here. The daemon creates the FIFO itself, so init
# only has to make the directory; 0755 because the controlling app reads it and
# an app uid is not in the daemon's group.
on post-fs-data
    # init re-owns the directory if it already exists under the old uid.
    mkdir /data/misc/airplay 0755 system_ext_airplay system_ext_airplay

# The quotes around the name matter. init tokenises the line before it
# expands anything, so an unquoted ${prop:-Jetson TV} splits at the space into
# "${persist.jetsontv.airplay.name:-Jetson" and "TV}", and expanding the first
# fails with "unexpected end of string ... looking for }". The service then
# exits with status 6 on every start and init restarts it forever. Quoting
# keeps it one token, and ${x:-default} expands normally after that.
service shairport-sync /system_ext/bin/shairport-sync -o aaudio --name "${persist.jetsontv.airplay.name:-Jetson TV}" --metadata-pipename=/data/misc/airplay/metadata
    class main
    user system_ext_airplay
    group system_ext_airplay inet
    disabled
    seclabel u:r:shairport:s0

on property:persist.jetsontv.airplay.enabled=true
    start shairport-sync

on property:persist.jetsontv.airplay.enabled=false
    stop shairport-sync
